%N A400004 Half the minimum surface area of a rectangular box with positive integer side lengths and volume at least n.
%C A400004 The minimum outside surface area of an integer-sided rectangular box that can hold n unit cubes, allowing unused space, is 2*a(n). Thus a(1)=3 corresponds to surface area 6 for a unit cube, and a(7)=12 corresponds to area 24 for a 2 X 2 X 2 box holding seven cubes. Equivalently, a(n) is the least possible sum of the areas of three mutually adjacent faces of such a box.
%C A400004 Unlike A075777, the box volume may exceed n. Unlike A193416, the shape must be a rectangular box. The sequence is nondecreasing.
%C A400004 The version allowing unused space was discussed by Kevin Karplus in comments on Dan Meyer's 2014 post and by Addison Stumpf and Jonah in comments on his 2015 post; see Links.
%H A400004 Scott B. Farrar, <a href="/A400004/b400004.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A400004 Dan Meyer, <a href="https://blog.mrmeyer.com/2014/purposeful-practice-dandy-candies/">Purposeful Practice & Dandy Candies</a> (2014). See comment 12 by gasstationwithoutpumps (Kevin Karplus), August 10, 2014, discussing unused capacity and an enumeration algorithm.
%H A400004 Dan Meyer, <a href="https://blog.mrmeyer.com/2015/the-math-problem-that-1000-math-teachers-couldnt-solve/">The Math Problem That 1,000 Math Teachers Couldn't Solve</a> (2015). See comments 135-136 by Addison Stumpf and Jonah, September 26, 2015, discussing the variant allowing empty spaces.
%H A400004 OEIS Wiki, <a href="https://oeis.org/wiki/A400K_Winners">A400K Winners</a>, 2026.
%H A400004 Jonathan Rotgé and Gérald Tenenbaum, <a href="https://tenenb.perso.math.cnrs.fr/PPP/on_integral_boxes.pdf">On integral boxes of minimal surface</a>, Journal of Number Theory 289 (2026), 85-95. Related work on boxes with prescribed exact volume.
%F A400004 a(n) = min{x*y + x*z + y*z : x,y,z are positive integers and x*y*z >= n}.
%F A400004 a(n) = min{A075777(m)/2 : n <= m <= ceiling(n^(1/3))^3}.
%F A400004 3*n^(2/3) <= a(n) <= 3*ceiling(n^(1/3))^2.
%F A400004 a(k^3) = 3*k^2 for k >= 1.
%F A400004 a(n) ~ 3*n^(2/3).
%e A400004 For n = 5, the box with dimensions 1,2,3 has volume 6 and surface area 22, so a(5) = 11. One unit of capacity is unused.
%e A400004 For n = 7, the 2 X 2 X 2 box has volume 8 and surface area 24, so a(7) = 12. A075777(7) = 30 because that sequence requires exact volume 7.
%e A400004 a(10) = a(11) = a(12) = 16, attained by the 2 X 2 X 3 box, which has surface area 32.
%t A400004 Clear[a];
%t A400004 a[n_Integer] /; n >= 1 := Module[{k, best, x, y, z},
%t A400004   k = Ceiling[n^(1/3)];
%t A400004   best = 3 k^2;
%t A400004   Do[
%t A400004     Do[
%t A400004       z = Max[y, Ceiling[n/(x y)]];
%t A400004       best = Min[best, x y + x z + y z],
%t A400004       {y, x, Floor[Sqrt[best + x^2]] - x}
%t A400004     ],
%t A400004     {x, 1, k}
%t A400004   ];
%t A400004   best
%t A400004 ];
%t A400004 Table[a[n], {n, 1, 64}]
%o A400004 (Python)
%o A400004 from math import isqrt
%o A400004 def ceil_cuberoot(n):
%o A400004     """Exact ceil(cube_root(n)) for a positive integer."""
%o A400004     if type(n) is not int or n < 1:
%o A400004         raise ValueError("n must be a positive integer")
%o A400004     lo, hi = 0, 1 << ((n.bit_length() + 2) // 3)
%o A400004     while lo + 1 < hi:
%o A400004         mid = (lo + hi) // 2
%o A400004         if mid ** 3 < n:
%o A400004             lo = mid
%o A400004         else:
%o A400004             hi = mid
%o A400004     return hi
%o A400004 def a(n):
%o A400004     """Minimum of x*y+x*z+y*z over positive integers x*y*z >= n."""
%o A400004     k = ceil_cuberoot(n)
%o A400004     best = 3 * k * k  # Half-area of a feasible k by k by k cube.
%o A400004     for x in range(1, k + 1):
%o A400004         # For x <= y <= z, half-area >= y*y + 2*x*y.
%o A400004         for y in range(x, isqrt(best + x*x) - x + 1):
%o A400004             z = max(y, (n + x*y - 1) // (x*y))
%o A400004             best = min(best, x*y + x*z + y*z)
%o A400004     return best
%o A400004 if __name__ == "__main__":
%o A400004     print([a(n) for n in range(1, 65)])
%Y A400004 Cf. A075777, A193416.
%K A400004 nonn,nice,new
%O A400004 1,1
